# Build context exclusions.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS THE HIGHEST-VALUE LINE IN THE PACKAGING AUDIT
#
# `docker/build.sh` runs `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile -t dp-code .` from
# the repository root, so the build context is the whole tree: 327 GB measured on
# 2026-08-05 (.datasets 231 GB, .scratch 95 GB, .git 1.4 GB, wandb 77 MB,
# papers 15 MB). Without this file every one of those bytes is streamed to the
# daemon before the build starts — to COPY a single 5 KB `requirements.txt`.
#
# The Dockerfile deliberately copies dependency manifests and nothing else: the
# source arrives by bind mount at run time (docker/run.sh), so baking it in would
# only be shadowed. Keep this list a denylist rather than `*` + un-ignores, so
# that adding a `COPY` to the Dockerfile does not silently copy nothing.

# --- the four that matter (in size order) ------------------------------------
.datasets/
.scratch/
.git/
wandb/

# --- other large or machine-local trees --------------------------------------
papers/
analysis/
results/
downloads/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Untracked vendored clones. project/UNI is 13 MB and must exist locally; the
# Hezil reference clone carries its own .git.
project/UNI/
project/Selective-Multimodal-Deep-Learning-for-Breast-Cancer-Subtype-Classification/

# --- run artifacts that were committed in the past ---------------------------
# These ARE tracked (435 MB of RNA-thread checkpoints under
# project/CLAM/results/, 5 MB under tmp_eval/) and are records of what was run,
# so they stay in git — but nothing in the image needs them.
project/CLAM/results/
project/CLAM/tmp_eval/
project/CLAM/heatmaps/
project/CLAM/wandb/

# --- ordinary noise ----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.vscode/
.claude/
.agents/
.openclaw/
.DS_Store
